ield. Finally, we discuss how we foresee holography contributing to compact-star physics in the coming years.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Elsevier B.V."}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"In this review article, we describe the role of holography in deciphering the physics of dense QCD matter, relevant for the description of compact stars and their binary mergers. We review the strengths and limitations of the holographic duality in describing strongly interacting matter at large baryon density, walk the reader through the most important results derived using the holographic approach so far, and highlight a number of outstanding open problems in the field. Finally, we discuss how we foresee holography contributing to compact-star physics in the coming years.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"control_number":1991905,"dois":[{"material":"publication","source":"Elsevier B.V.","value":"10.1016/j.ppnp.2022.103972"},{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1016/j.ppnp.2022.103972"}],"preprint_date":"2021-12-15","arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["hep-th","astro-ph.HE","gr-qc","hep-ph","nucl-th"],"value":"2112.08422"}],"titles":[{"source":"Elsevier B.V.","title":"Holographic approach to compact stars and their binary mergers"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Holographic approach to compact stars and their binary mergers"}],"document_type":["article"]},"id":"1991905"}],"total":1},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2112.08422&size=5&page=1&fields=titles,authors,dois,publication_info,arxiv_eprints,document_type,preprint_date,imprints,abstracts,urls","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2112.08422&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2112.08422&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2112.08422&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2112.08422&size=5&